Package: lm15
Title: One Interface to Many Language Model Providers
Version: 1.1.2
Authors@R: person("Maxime", "Rivest", email = "mrive052@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Builds one request for many language model providers ('OpenAI',
    'Anthropic', 'Google Gemini', 'xAI', 'Microsoft Azure', 'Amazon Bedrock',
    'Google Vertex AI', hosted open models, and local servers such as
    'Ollama' and 'vLLM') and returns the same typed response, stream events
    and errors from each. Provider differences are translated at one
    boundary: a setting a provider cannot accept is adapted and recorded on
    the response, or refused before sending, and never dropped silently.
    Also covers tools, structured output, judgments with probabilities,
    files, batches, prompt caches, image, speech and video generation, live
    sessions, and subscription sign-in. Implements the same contract as the
    'Python', 'TypeScript', 'Rust' and 'Go' implementations
    <https://lm15.dev>.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://lm15.dev, https://github.com/lm15-dev/lm15-r
BugReports: https://github.com/lm15-dev/lm15-r/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: askpass, curl, jsonlite, openssl, stats, utils
Suggests: callr, httpuv, knitr, later, pkgload, processx, rmarkdown,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0), xml2
VignetteBuilder: knitr
SystemRequirements: libcurl (>= 7.86.0) with WebSocket support, optional:
    used for live sessions only
Config/testthat/edition: 3
